<VALID_PLOTLY_PATTERNS>

IMPORTANT: Only use valid Plotly properties. Here are proven patterns:

**Bar Chart:**
```python
import plotly.graph_objects as go

fig = go.Figure(data=[
    go.Bar(
        x=['Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4'],
        y=[2.3, 2.8, 3.1, 3.9],
        marker_color='#1e88e5',
        marker_line_color='#1565c0',
        marker_line_width=1,
        text=[2.3, 2.8, 3.1, 3.9],
        textposition='outside',
        texttemplate='%{text:.1f}M',
        width=0.6
    )
])
fig.update_layout(
    title=dict(text='Chart Title', font=dict(size=20, color='#2c3e50')),
    xaxis=dict(title='X Label', tickfont=dict(size=12)),
    yaxis=dict(title='Y Label', tickfont=dict(size=12)),
    plot_bgcolor='white',
    paper_bgcolor='white',
    margin=dict(t=60, b=60, l=60, r=40),
    bargap=0.2,  # NOTE: bargap is a LAYOUT property, not a Bar property
    showlegend=False
)
fig.update_xaxes(showgrid=False, showline=True, linecolor='#e0e0e0')
fig.update_yaxes(showgrid=True, gridcolor='#f0f0f0', showline=True, linecolor='#e0e0e0')
```

**Line Chart:**
```python
import plotly.graph_objects as go

fig = go.Figure(data=[
    go.Scatter(
        x=['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar'],
        y=[10, 15, 13],
        mode='lines+markers',
        line=dict(color='#1e88e5', width=3),
        marker=dict(size=8, color='#1e88e5')
    )
])
```

**Pie Chart:**
```python
import plotly.graph_objects as go

fig = go.Figure(data=[
    go.Pie(
        labels=['A', 'B', 'C'],
        values=[30, 50, 20],
        hole=0.4,
        marker=dict(colors=['#1e88e5', '#42a5f5', '#90caf9']),
        textinfo='percent+label'
    )
])
```

**INVALID PROPERTIES TO AVOID:**
- marker.smoothing (does not exist)
- line.smoothing on Bar charts (only valid on Scatter with shape='spline')
- marker.cornerradius (does not exist)
- bargap on go.Bar() - THIS IS A LAYOUT PROPERTY, use fig.update_layout(bargap=0.2)
- Any property not in Plotly documentation

**REMEMBER:**
- bargap, bargroupgap are LAYOUT properties, not trace properties
- Always put them in fig.update_layout(), never in go.Bar()

</VALID_PLOTLY_PATTERNS>

